From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:11:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable dark palette and focus outline for Phone

The Sable Phone design (sable-phone-dialer-titan2) is dark only. Phone
now uses one dark palette whatever the system light/dark setting,
instead of a light theme that the platform force-darkens at night:

* sable_colors.xml carries the Sable dark tokens (SableSystemTokens.Dark
  surfaces and text, SableTheme's outline tones, success and danger).
  The accent is not hard-coded: sable_accent and its container are
  system_accent1_200 / system_accent1_900, which the Sable accent seeds.
* The Dialer base theme now inherits Theme.AppCompat (dark), never
  force-darkens, and its colour resources point at the tokens:
  near-black window, slightly lighter surfaces for the bottom bar,
  dial pad and search pill, raised panels for cards, sheets and
  dialogs, light primary and muted secondary text, dark status and
  navigation bars. The -night copies of those resources are removed,
  as they would now repeat the defaults.
* The theme's selectableItemBackground is a Sable row background: a
  ripple for touch and, while the row has keyboard or trackpad focus,
  a 2dp accent outline around a dark accent fill (12dp corners). Rows
  that use it upstream (contacts tab, search results, Recents actions,
  favourites, suggestions, settings) get the outline; the bottom bar
  tabs use it too.
* In-call: the background is the near-black base, checked controls use
  the accent, End and the RTT end tint use the danger tone.
* Favourite action sheet and promotion sheet: their hard-coded white
  backgrounds follow the floating surface; bottom sheets use the dark
  Material sheet theme.

No Java change. Focus order, touch targets and every upstream function
are unchanged.
